# Force LF for every text file Git recognizes. This is the actual fix for
# the CRLF issue that broke `bash -n` on a raw checkout (bootstrap.sh,
# lib/system.sh): without this, CRLF can come back the moment anyone edits
# a file on Windows or has core.autocrlf=true, and CI goes red for a
# line-ending reason that has nothing to do with the code itself.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit per-extension rules on top of the catch-all above. Redundant with
# `text=auto eol=lf` for files Git already detects as text, but listed
# explicitly so intent isn't left to Git's heuristic alone for the file
# types this project actually ships and that CI reads (scripts, workflow
# manifest, CI config, docs).
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf

# Binary — never touch line endings.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
*.safetensors binary
